    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (81.27) leading the charge as our premier offensive anchor. Facing a weak arm in Palmquist, **Trea Turner** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP Skill and a favorable lineup slot, but his true value lies in the 100% stolen base probability projection against a slow delivery, which is critical given our pursuit of the league-leading SB category. He is closely shadowed by **Yordan Alvarez** (77.03) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84), both of whom exploit advantageous platoon splits and high-skill matchups. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core piece due to his elite 0.448 xwOBA, while **Christian Yelich** leverages a 13% dynamic platoon boost and a matchup against a soft SP_xERA of 5.10 to maximize our R and RBI potential.\n\nMid-tier production will be anchored by **Caleb Durbin** (67.14), who provides crucial speed upside with a 90% stolen base indicator against Freeland, alongside **Junior Caminero** (58.80) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (57.98), both of whom are poised for solid output despite moderate park factors. **Luke Raley** (41.50) stands as our most significant bench decision; while he cleared our internal efficiency floor, his output was stifled by a difficult matchup against Ashcraft and a low batting order position, ultimately forcing him to the bench in favor of more efficient platoon-advantaged bats. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (45.60); his score is dragging near the threshold due to a significant -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Manaea, and he remains a high-risk start if his role is diminished late in the day. We are currently tracking roster availability for **Rece Hinds** and **Hyeseong Kim**, both of whom remain in the minors and are unavailable for selection.",
